Cortex v0.6.0 -- Local agent memory

Usage: cortex <command> [--home <path>] [--db <path>]

  capture <register|enable|disable|put|tail|get> [--quiet]
  capabilities --json      Discover local operations
  status [--json]           Open and inspect the local brain
  setup                    Configure MCP clients and initialize memory
  mcp [--agent <name>]      MCP stdio, in-process
  boot [--agent <name>] [--budget <n>] [--json]
  op <operation> [--args '<json>'] [--agent <name>]
  maintain [--jobs <n>]     Drain a bounded maintenance slice
  serve                    Optional headless maintenance worker, no listener
  paths --json             Show local paths
  hook-boot [--agent <name>] | hook-status | hook-event <kind>
  prompt-inject --file <path> [--agent <name>] [--budget <n>] [--watch]
  doctor | backup | restore <file>
  cleanup [--dry-run] [--events] [--max-passes <n>]
  reindex [--json] | recrystallize [--json]
  rebuild-anchors [--json] [--batch-size <n>]
  embeddings status [--json] | eval | robot-docs guide

No network endpoint, background service, or remote API key is required.
